# node_modules is the one that matters, and the reason is not the obvious one. The
# image installs its own tree from the lock file; a host tree copied in carries the
# wrong platform's binding for rolldown's native parser (vite 8 bundles with rolldown).
#
# That does not fail, which is why it needs excluding rather than trusting. Checked by
# mounting this checkout's darwin-arm64 tree into the linux image: rolldown silently
# falls back to its wasm32-wasi build -- npm installs that one unconditionally, so it is
# always there -- and the server comes up on the slower parser, announced by nothing but
# four "ExperimentalWarning: WASI is an experimental feature" warnings. A hard error
# would be easier to notice.
node_modules/

# Build output. Nothing in the compose stack serves it (the dev server is the server),
# and a stale copy in the image would only be confusing.
dist/
.vite/

.env
.env.*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
.DS_Store
*.log
